IO-24: read the rain barrel Covrd token on [LID_CONTROLS] STORAGE lines

The STORAGE parser read only the four numbers, so the fifth token (YES/NO)
was dropped and LIDGroupSoA::stor_covered stayed 0: every rain barrel was
uncovered, and the covered-barrel branch of stepRunoff() never ran. Store
the flag next to the four numbers (STORAGE[4], set as legacy readStorageData
does: covered only for YES, uncovered when the token is absent), copy it to
stor_covered, and write YES back in the .inp writer.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-24_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/InpWriter.cpp b/src/engine/core/InpWriter.cpp
index 8c5f986..14df1a9 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/InpWriter.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/InpWriter.cpp
@@ -2143,6 +2143,8 @@ int writeInpFile(const SimulationContext&  ctx_internal,
                 if (has) {
                     std::fprintf(f,"%-16s STORAGE    ", name);
                     for (int k=0;k<4;++k) std::fprintf(f," %10.4f",p[k]);
+                    if (uj < ctx.lid_controls.storage_covered.size() &&
+                        ctx.lid_controls.storage_covered[uj]) std::fprintf(f," YES");
                     std::fprintf(f,"\n");
                 }
             }
